================================================================================
Third-party runtime dependencies
================================================================================

The following packages are installed as runtime dependencies when you install
`HomericIntelligence-Hephaestus`. Their licenses are listed below; each is
compatible with BSD 3-Clause distribution because they are imported, not
modified or redistributed.

These determinations are machine-enforced on every PR by the `license-scan`
CI job (scripts/check_license_compatibility.py), which installs the package
with all runtime extras (`pip install -e .[all]`) and scans the DISTRIBUTED
dependency set (base + runtime extras, not dev tooling). A new distributed
dependency under an incompatible license, an unrecognized license string, or a
missing runtime extra fails CI. When you add a non-vendored copyleft extra
here, also add it to that script's ALLOWED_EXTRA_COPYLEFT map.

  Jinja2        BSD-3-Clause
  packaging     Apache-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause
  pyyaml        MIT
  pydantic      MIT
  tzdata        Apache-2.0 (packaging; bundles public-domain IANA tz database
                data — installed only on Windows: platform_system == 'Windows')

================================================================================
Optional (extras) runtime dependencies
================================================================================

These packages are installed only when the corresponding extra is requested
(e.g. `pip install HomericIntelligence-Hephaestus[github]`):

  nats extra
    nats-py     Apache-2.0

  xml extra
    defusedxml  PSF-2.0

  schema extra
    jsonschema  MIT

